    "sideEffects": "**Prominent short-term-only cautions (read carefully):** **Use only short-term** (commonly on the order of **up to about 1 week** unless a clinician directs otherwise) for occasional constipation. Cramping, urgency, and loose stools are expected pharmacology—not \"toxins exiting.\" **Chronic use:** dependency (cathartic colon), **potassium loss**, dehydration, rebound constipation. **Do not use** with undiagnosed abdominal pain, vomiting, suspected obstruction/appendicitis, or IBD flare without clinician clearance. **Pregnancy:** stimulant laxatives generally avoided unless obstetric clinician specifically recommends. **Nursing:** discuss with clinician. **Drug/electrolyte interactions:** hypokalemia risk discussions with diuretics and digoxin—pharmacist review. **Eating-disorder misuse:** dangerous—seek appropriate care. Fresh (unaged) bark traditionally considered harsher—commercial aged bark exists for a reason. Educational only—**not** a detox, weight-loss, or daily wellness purge. Apenas educativo — não é aconselhamento médico.",
